Definition of Plea Bargain:

An agreement between a criminal defendant and a prosecutor in which
the defendant admits having committed a crime. In return, the
prosecutor asks the judge to impose a less severe sentence than
had the defendant been convicted at a trial. The judge is not bound
by the terms of a plea bargain. A plea bargain ensures that a
guilty defendant is punished.
http://www.bereamunicourt.org/info.asp

To agree to a guilty plea to a less serious charge in order to have
a more serious charge dropped.
http://www.nationaltcc.org/tcc/

For more definition of Plea Bargain, see
http://www.google.com/search?hl=en&lr=&oi=defmore&q=define:Plea+bargain

